*> Contract test, the client's consumer side of the protocol codec (contracts/proto-api.md §1, §2,
*> §5): PB-BUFFER and the PROTO.cpy records the client uses (PB-ITEMSTACK, PB-TEXT) have the lengths
*> and layout of §1; each PB-*, NBT-*, CHUNK-* and LIGHT-* program the client calls links and gives
*> back on a minimal valid call what was written (§5 parameters).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. CLIENT-CONTRACT-PROTO-CONSUMER.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY PROTO REPLACING LEADING ==PB-== BY ==FR-==.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 256.
 01 WS-INT                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-INT2                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-INT3                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LONG                BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-DOUBLE              FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-FLOAT               FLOAT-SHORT.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(32).
 01 WS-TEXT-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CAP                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 32.
 01 WS-MAX                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 32.
 01 WS-UUID                PIC X(16) VALUE "0123456789ABCDEF".
 01 WS-OUT                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-PTR                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-E                   PIC -(9)9.
 01 WN                     PIC X(16).
 01 WL                     BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TEN                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 10.
 01 WS-ELEMENT             BINARY-LONG VALUE -1.
 01 WS-STRING-TYPE         BINARY-LONG VALUE 8.
 01 WS-ONE                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-FILE-FRAMING        BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-PATH                PIC X(64) VALUE "build/client-test-proto.dat".
 01 WS-PATH-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG VALUE 27.
 01 WS-OUTCOME             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-THRESHOLD           BINARY-LONG VALUE 16.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FIVE                BINARY-LONG VALUE 5.
 01 WS-TWO                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 2.
 01 WS-STATES.
    05 WS-ST               BINARY-LONG OCCURS 4096 TIMES.
 01 WS-STATES2.
    05 WS-ST2              BINARY-LONG OCCURS 4096 TIMES.
 01 WS-BIOMES.
    05 WS-BI               BINARY-LONG OCCURS 64 TIMES.
 01 WS-FOUR-K              BINARY-LONG VALUE 4096.
 01 WS-LIGHTS              BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-SKY-STATES.
    05 WS-SKY-STATE        BINARY-LONG OCCURS 3 TIMES.
 01 WS-BLOCK-STATES.
    05 WS-BLOCK-STATE      BINARY-LONG OCCURS 3 TIMES.
 01 WS-SKY-ARRAYS.
    05 WS-SKY-ARRAY        PIC X(2048) OCCURS 3 TIMES.
 01 WS-BLOCK-ARRAYS.
    05 WS-BLOCK-ARRAY      PIC X(2048) OCCURS 3 TIMES.
 01 WS-BYTES               PIC X(8) VALUE "ABCDEFGH".
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 B-FRAME                PIC X(256) BASED.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "contract client proto consumer PB-BUFFER is 21 bytes, PB-ITEMSTACK 8, PB-TEXT 9257"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 2100089257 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = FUNCTION LENGTH(PB-BUFFER) * 100000000
         + FUNCTION LENGTH(PB-ITEMSTACK) * 10000 + FUNCTION LENGTH(PB-TEXT)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Scalars: written with PB-PUT-*, read back with PB-GET-*.
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     MOVE 300 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     MOVE -5 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-BYTE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     MOVE 200 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-UBYTE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     MOVE 25565 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-USHORT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     MOVE 1762300800000 TO WS-LONG
     CALL "PB-PUT-LONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LONG
     MOVE 4.5 TO WS-DOUBLE
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-DOUBLE
     MOVE 9.0 TO WS-FLOAT
     CALL "PB-PUT-FLOAT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-FLOAT
     MOVE "en_us" TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE 5 TO WS-TEXT-LENGTH
     CALL "PB-PUT-STRING" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TEXT WS-TEXT-LENGTH WS-MAX
     MOVE "minecraft:brand" TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE 15 TO WS-TEXT-LENGTH
     CALL "PB-PUT-IDENTIFIER" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TEXT WS-TEXT-LENGTH
     CALL "PB-PUT-UUID" USING PB-BUFFER WS-UUID
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES WS-TWO
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OUT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-BYTE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-UBYTE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE 2 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-SKIP" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-LONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LONG
     MOVE WS-LONG TO WS-INT
     COMPUTE WS-INT = WS-LONG / 1000000
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-DOUBLE
     COMPUTE WS-INT = WS-DOUBLE * 10
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-FLOAT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-FLOAT
     MOVE WS-FLOAT TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-STRING" USING PB-BUFFER WS-MAX WS-TEXT WS-CAP WS-TEXT-LENGTH
     STRING " " WS-TEXT(1:WS-TEXT-LENGTH) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OUT WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     CALL "PB-GET-IDENTIFIER" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TEXT WS-CAP WS-TEXT-LENGTH
     STRING " " WS-TEXT(1:WS-TEXT-LENGTH) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OUT WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     MOVE 16 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-SKIP" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     MOVE ZERO TO WS-INT
     MOVE "contract client proto consumer scalars round-trip (VarInt, Bool, Byte, UByte, UShort "
         & "skipped, Long, Double, Float, String, Identifier, UUID skipped)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE " 300 1 -5 200 1762300 45 9 en_us minecraft:brand 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE WS-OUT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Composite reads the client makes: Int, VarLong, Position, ItemStack, Text.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE X"00000007" TO WS-BYTES(1:4)
     MOVE 4 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES WS-INT
     MOVE X"F02E" TO WS-BYTES(1:2)
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES WS-TWO
     MOVE X"0000010000008036" TO WS-BYTES
     MOVE 8 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES WS-INT
     MOVE X"3F020000" TO WS-BYTES(1:4)
     MOVE 4 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES WS-INT
     MOVE X"08000378797A" TO WS-BYTES(1:6)
     MOVE 6 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES WS-INT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OUT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     CALL "PB-GET-INT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-VARLONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LONG
     MOVE WS-LONG TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-POSITION" USING PB-BUFFER WS-X WS-Y WS-Z
     MOVE WS-X TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE WS-Y TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE WS-Z TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-ITEMSTACK" USING PB-BUFFER PB-ITEMSTACK
     MOVE PB-IS-COUNT TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE PB-IS-ITEM TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-TEXT" USING PB-BUFFER PB-TEXT
     STRING " " PB-TX-VALUE(1:PB-TX-LENGTH) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OUT WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     MOVE "contract client proto consumer reads Int 7, VarLong 6000, Position (4, 54, 8), an "
         & "ItemStack 63 x 2 and a plain Text" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE " 7 6000 4 54 8 63 2 xyz" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-OUT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   NBT written and read back, through a gzip NBT file.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE SPACES TO WN
     MOVE 0 TO WL
     CALL "NBT-WRITE-COMPOUND-BEGIN" USING PB-BUFFER WN WL
     MOVE "List" TO WN
     MOVE 4 TO WL
     CALL "NBT-WRITE-LIST-BEGIN" USING PB-BUFFER WN WL WS-STRING-TYPE WS-ONE
     MOVE "abc" TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE 3 TO WS-TEXT-LENGTH
     CALL "NBT-WRITE-STRING" USING PB-BUFFER WN WS-ELEMENT WS-TEXT WS-TEXT-LENGTH
     MOVE "N" TO WN
     MOVE 1 TO WL
     CALL "NBT-WRITE-INT" USING PB-BUFFER WN WL WS-TEN
     CALL "NBT-WRITE-COMPOUND-END" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "NBT-FILE-WRITE" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH PB-BUFFER WS-OUTCOME
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "NBT-FILE-READ" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH PB-BUFFER WS-INT2
     CALL "NBT-READ-ROOT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-FILE-FRAMING WS-TYPE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OUT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     MOVE WS-OUTCOME TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE WS-INT2 TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE SPACES TO WN
     CALL "NBT-READ-COMPOUND-NEXT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TYPE WN WS-CAP WL
     CALL "NBT-READ-LIST-BEGIN" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TYPE WS-COUNT
     CALL "NBT-READ-STRING" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TEXT WS-CAP WS-TEXT-LENGTH
     STRING " " WN(1:WL) " " WS-TEXT(1:WS-TEXT-LENGTH) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OUT
         WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     MOVE SPACES TO WN
     CALL "NBT-READ-COMPOUND-NEXT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TYPE WN WS-CAP WL
     CALL "NBT-READ-SKIP" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TYPE
     CALL "NBT-READ-COMPOUND-NEXT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TYPE WN WS-CAP WL
     MOVE WS-TYPE TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE "contract client proto consumer NBT written to a gzip file and read back: List [abc], "
         & "an Int skipped, End" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE " 0 0 List abc 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-OUT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   A frame encoded and decoded with threshold 16; a chunk section and light round trip.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE 13 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING FR-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "PB-FRAME-ENCODE" USING FR-BUFFER PB-BUFFER WS-THRESHOLD
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-FRAME-DECODE" USING FR-BUFFER PB-BUFFER WS-THRESHOLD WS-ZERO WS-ID WS-OUTCOME
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OUT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     MOVE WS-ID TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE WS-OUTCOME TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-INT FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-INT > 4096
         COMPUTE WS-ST(WS-INT) = FUNCTION MOD(WS-INT, 3) + 2
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BI(1)
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "CHUNK-SECTION-ENCODE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-FOUR-K WS-ZERO WS-STATES WS-BIOMES WS-FIVE
         WS-TWO
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SKY-STATE(1) WS-BLOCK-STATE(1) WS-BLOCK-STATE(2) WS-BLOCK-STATE(3)
         WS-SKY-STATE(3)
     MOVE 2 TO WS-SKY-STATE(2)
     MOVE ALL X"FF" TO WS-SKY-ARRAY(2)
     CALL "LIGHT-ENCODE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LIGHTS WS-SKY-STATES WS-SKY-ARRAYS WS-BLOCK-STATES
         WS-BLOCK-ARRAYS
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "CHUNK-SECTION-DECODE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-FIVE WS-TWO WS-INT2 WS-INT3 WS-STATES2
         WS-BIOMES
     MOVE WS-ST2(4096) TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE ALL X"00" TO WS-SKY-ARRAY(2)
     CALL "LIGHT-DECODE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LIGHTS WS-SKY-STATES WS-SKY-ARRAYS WS-BLOCK-STATES
         WS-BLOCK-ARRAYS
     MOVE WS-SKY-STATE(2) TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-INT
     PERFORM SHOW-INT
     MOVE "contract client proto consumer a frame round-trips (Client Tick End, threshold 16); a "
         & "chunk section and its light decode" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE " 13 0 3 2 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     IF WS-SKY-ARRAY(2) NOT = ALL X"FF"
         MOVE "sky array lost" TO TL-EXPECTED
     END-IF
     MOVE WS-OUT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING FR-BUFFER
     STOP RUN.

 SHOW-INT.
     MOVE WS-INT TO WS-E
     STRING " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OUT WITH POINTER WS-PTR.
 END PROGRAM CLIENT-CONTRACT-PROTO-CONSUMER.
